<%= header_section("Auto-flagged: sales far exceeding page views") %>
<div>
  <p>
    Product:
    <%= link_to @product.name, admin_product_url(@product.unique_permalink) %>
  </p>

  <p>
    In the previous hour this product recorded <strong><%= number_with_delimiter(@sales_count) %></strong> free sales
    against <strong><%= number_with_delimiter(@views_count) %></strong> product page views. Sales running that far
    ahead of views means the checkouts did not come through the product page, which is what
    scripted checkouts look like. Every one of them sends a receipt from our transactional
    sending domain to whatever address the script supplied.
  </p>

  <p>
    The product has already been unpublished, so no further checkouts can go through it. The
    seller has been flagged for review. No action is needed to stop the sends — the decision
    here is whether to suspend the account or clear it and republish the product.
  </p>

  <p>Creator:</p>
  <%= render("admin_mailer/internal_user_info", user: @user) %>
</div>
